@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# Venzo Store API contract
+
+The Android app talks only to the public Venzo Store API. It must never call
+the PasarGuard admin API or contain PasarGuard credentials.
+
+## Android build setting
+
+Build with the public HTTPS origin:
+
+```text
+--dart-define=VENZO_API_BASE=https://api.example.com
+```
+
+## Public routes
+
+### `GET /v1/plans`
+
+```json
+{
+  "plans": [
+    {
+      "id": "monthly-20",
+      "title": "یک‌ماهه ۲۰ گیگ",
+      "price": 600000,
+      "currency": "IRR",
+      "days": 30,
+      "data_gb": 20
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### `POST /v1/orders`
+
+Request:
+
+```json
+{
+  "plan_id": "monthly-20",
+  "customer": "@customer",
+  "client": "venzo-android"
+}
+```
+
+Response:
+
+```json
+{
+  "order_id": "vz_123",
+  "checkout_url": "https://pay.example.com/vz_123"
+}
+```
+
+## Backend responsibilities
+
+1. Validate the plan server-side; never trust price, duration, or traffic from
+   the app.
+2. Create a pending order and return a short-lived HTTPS checkout URL.
+3. Verify the payment provider callback server-to-server and make processing
+   idempotent by payment authority/transaction ID.
+4. Only after verified payment, authenticate to PasarGuard with server-side
+   credentials and create/renew the user with the plan's traffic and expiry.
+5. Store the returned `subscription_url` against the order for later secure
+   delivery to the customer.
+6. Apply rate limits, audit logging, and strict CORS/body-size limits. Never
+   return the PasarGuard bearer token or admin credentials to the app.
+
+PasarGuard is the subscription/provisioning system; it does not replace the
+payment gateway. The payment gateway and its callback credentials must be
+chosen before the purchase flow can be activated in production.
